\title{DentalClaw: A Modular Platform for Standardized and Auditable Dental Imaging Artificial Intelligence Workflows}

%% Abstract
\begin{abstract}
\textit{Objectives:} Dental imaging artificial intelligence (AI) research is increasingly important in digital dentistry, but many dentists and clinical researchers face technical barriers in dataset preparation, model execution, evaluation, and reproducible reporting. This study aimed to develop and validate DentalClaw, a natural-language-driven platform that converts user research intent into standardized, executable, and reviewable dental imaging AI workflows.\\
\textit{Methods:} DentalClaw was implemented as a modular platform integrating natural-language task orchestration, dataset curation, quality checking, train--test split verification, model execution, standardized evaluation, and structured reporting. Large-language-model-guided orchestration was used to translate user instructions into executable workflows, while deterministic modules performed data processing, training, inference, evaluation, and logging. Workflow validation was conducted on two representative tasks: 2D panoramic radiograph segmentation and 3D cone-beam computed tomography (CBCT) segmentation. An exploratory private panoramic radiograph object-detection workflow was also included to assess extensibility to clinical data and lesion-focused refinement.\\
\textit{Results:} DentalClaw completed end-to-end workflows for both 2D panoramic radiograph and 3D CBCT segmentation tasks, from dataset preparation to model training, inference, evaluation, and structured reporting. Compared with manually assembled workflows, the platform reduced manual coordination during dataset preparation and result organization while producing comparable task-level segmentation results. It also generated reproducible artifacts, including workflow metadata, split files, prediction outputs, evaluation tables, and review-oriented reports. These results support the feasibility of natural-language-guided orchestration for standardized and traceable dental imaging AI experimentation.\\
\textit{Conclusions:} DentalClaw demonstrated the feasibility of natural-language-guided orchestration for standardized and auditable dental imaging AI workflows. By integrating dataset preparation, model execution, evaluation, reporting, and exploratory private-data refinement into a unified workflow, the platform may reduce manual coordination burden and improve the reproducibility and reviewability of dental AI experimentation.\\
\textit{Clinical Significance:} DentalClaw may help dentists and clinical researchers participate more directly in panoramic radiograph and CBCT AI studies by lowering technical barriers while preserving traceable and reviewable workflow outputs.
\end{abstract}

